# Document Management System for a Law Firm
Case study: Faculty of Law, University of Ibadan (CSC 467, Group 35)
PHP 8 + MySQL web application that implements the design in Chapter Three and the modules described in Chapter Four.

## 1. Set it up on your PC (about 10 minutes)

1. Install **XAMPP** (https://www.apachefriends.org). Choose the version with PHP 8.x.
2. Open the **XAMPP Control Panel** and click **Start** next to **Apache** and **MySQL**. Both should turn green.
3. Copy this whole folder (rename it `dms`) into `C:\xampp\htdocs\` so you have `C:\xampp\htdocs\dms\login.php`.
4. In your browser open **http://localhost/dms/install.php** and click **Install now**.
   This creates the database `dms_law`, the 10 tables, and sample (fictional) data.
5. Note the usernames and passwords shown on the page, then click **Go to the login page**.
6. After installing, **delete `install.php`** from the folder.

Uploaded documents are saved in `C:\xampp\dms_storage` (outside `htdocs`), so a browser can never request a stored file directly. Files are only served by `download.php` after a permission check.

### If something goes wrong
| Problem | Fix |
|---|---|
| "Cannot connect to MySQL" | Start MySQL in the XAMPP Control Panel. If port 3306 is busy, stop other MySQL services or change the port. |
| Blank page or "Call to undefined function" | Use a PHP 8 version of XAMPP. In `C:\xampp\php\php.ini` make sure `extension=pdo_mysql` and `extension=mbstring` are not commented out (no `;` in front), then restart Apache. |
| Upload fails for big files | In `php.ini` raise `upload_max_filesize` and `post_max_size` (XAMPP's default is 40M), then restart Apache. |
| "document storage folder could not be created" | Create the folder `C:\xampp\dms_storage` yourself, or make the project folder writable (the system then uses `dms\storage`). |
| Want a fresh start | In phpMyAdmin (http://localhost/phpmyadmin) drop the database `dms_law`, delete `C:\xampp\dms_storage`, then open `install.php` again (restore it from your original copy if you deleted it). |

