## 5. What is where
- `login.php`, `logout.php`, `dashboard.php` - authentication and dashboards for each role
- `users.php`, `audit.php`, `reports.php`, `backup.php` - Administrator (and reports for Lawyers)
- `clients.php`, `cases.php`, `case_view.php` - clients and case files
- `upload.php`, `documents.php`, `document.php`, `download.php`, `search.php` - documents, versions, search
- `hearings.php` - hearing diary and reminders
- `database/schema.sql` - the 10 tables (Chapter Three, Tables 3.8 - 3.17)
- `includes/` - shared code (database, access rules, audit trail, layout)

## 6. Security measures built in
Passwords stored with PHP `password_hash` (bcrypt); prepared statements (SQL injection); output escaping (XSS); CSRF token on every form; role-based access control checked on every page and file download; account lock after 5 failed logins; session expiry after 30 minutes; uploaded files renamed, stored outside the web root, SHA-256 hash recorded and re-checked on download; every important action written to the audit trail.

